<invention-title id="d2e43">Energy-aware scheduling of neural network training jobs</invention-title>
<us-parties>
<us-applicants>
<us-applicant sequence="00" app-type="applicant" designation="us-only" applicant-authority-category="assignee">
<addressbook>
<orgname>Quillfeather Compute, Inc.</orgname>
<address><city>Seattle</city><state>WA</state><country>US</country></address>
</addressbook>
<residence><country>US</country></residence>
</us-applicant>
</us-applicants>
<inventors>
<inventor sequence="00" designation="us-only">
<addressbook>
<last-name>Iyer</last-name>
<first-name>Meera</first-name>
<address><city>Seattle</city><state>WA</state><country>US</country></address>
</addressbook>
</inventor>
</inventors>
</us-parties>
</us-bibliographic-data-application>
<abstract id="abstract">
<p id="p-0001" num="0000">A scheduler forecasts grid carbon intensity and shifts checkpointed training jobs to low-intensity windows while meeting a deadline expressed as a service-level objective.</p>
</abstract>
<claims id="claims">
<claim id="CLM-00001" num="00001">
<claim-text>1. A method comprising forecasting a carbon intensity of a power grid and scheduling a checkpointed training job into a time window having a forecast intensity below a threshold.</claim-text>
</claim>
<claim id="CLM-00002" num="00002">
<claim-text>2. The method of <claim-ref idref="CLM-00001">claim 1</claim-ref>, wherein the job is preempted at a checkpoint when the intensity rises above the threshold.</claim-text>
</claim>
</claims>
</us-patent-application>
